{"id": "EUVD-2026-59659", "enisaUuid": "5768c07a-8a7c-34e8-b478-8b58db7d4295", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/zcrypt: Close speculative mem read possibility\n\nThe domain value is extracted from a given CCA or EP11 ioctl struct\nwhen a CPRB is about to be sent. Thus this is a user controlled value.\nUnder some special conditions (custom device node used, administrative\nload) this value is used as an array index after bounds checking, but\nwithout speculation barrier.\n\nAdd the missing array_index_nospec() call to prevent speculative\nexecution where this domain value is used.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T12:27:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:41", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd1a334523ba533cba63caf593a7329d8e0e5e6e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d11a260bd7dfc6f6ccd43e1b930050f24e70cd5f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/59adeedebf02aa1c203de1d2b67ec45bfab7a3c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/82b62eda68abfb7a33ac40f24b8c4128c2891148", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e935cd525af4c6ed2e2c6404aa27ca19c7f39ddb"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4w55-4rvm-3v48", "CVE-2026-74466"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "200b04da-475c-3959-b8db-4dca349b9e6d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "3df4e5cc-af5f-327d-8eae-36bb11949992", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cfd68b33094e1a92249850ff3c3c92ae9112a541 <82b62eda68abfb7a33ac40f24b8c4128c2891148"}, {"id": "566a813c-d2fc-372a-8963-bac04b797848", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "59f96c60-2875-347d-8a4a-9b17b429d500", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "793a7213-d10f-3ac0-abe6-29e1a3e72db2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "produc